      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that you’d see it that way—when the universe feels indifferent, the idea of \"meaning\" can seem like a story we tell ourselves. But the fact that you're asking this question shows you're still searching for something, even if it's buried under the weight of it all. Meaning isn't handed to us; it's built in small moments, connections, and choices that matter to *you*, even if they don't matter to the cosmos. If you're feeling this stuck, please reach out to someone who can sit with you in it—you don't have to figure it out alone.",
